00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:15.860
So the first thing is that
it's extremely interesting.

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:18.570
People like to learn throughout history.

00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:22.679
Progress in the world has come
from people being curious about

00:01:22.685 --> 00:01:24.480
things, wanting to learn things.

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:28.140
It's a natural sort of
instinct that we have.

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:30.450
We want to understand things,
we wanna learn things.

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:36.270
And so languages, learning languages
is a very enjoyable thing to do.

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:39.930
It's basically a natural
impulse that we have.

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:41.340
So that's reason number one.

00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:43.230
It's an enjoyable thing to do.

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:51.600
Reason number two, learning a language is
something that is available to all of us.

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:54.060
We don't have to have a special talent.

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:59.730
We don't need to be able to run
fast or jump high or sing well.

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:04.279
We follow our natural instincts.

00:02:04.679 --> 00:02:06.899
Instincts that we have from birth.

00:02:07.169 --> 00:02:12.450
The ability of the brain to be stimulated
and gradually develop new patterns to

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:18.480
cope with the experience that the brain
is, is coming up against and finding

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:20.370
ways to deal with this new situation.

00:02:20.549 --> 00:02:21.690
The brain can learn.

00:02:22.109 --> 00:02:23.609
The brain is made to learn.

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:26.160
The brain is made to create patterns.

00:02:26.835 --> 00:02:32.415
The brain learns slowly, but everybody's
brain can learn, so it's enjoyable.

00:02:32.505 --> 00:02:33.615
We can all do it.

00:02:33.795 --> 00:02:36.015
Those are two good reasons
to learn a language.

00:02:36.075 --> 00:02:40.965
The third thing is, and I'm gonna check
